From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO Fire Button

Add "Burn tabs and data" to the app menu (also in the tab switcher).
After a confirmation it closes all tabs, also the incognito and archived
tabs, without keeping them in Recent tabs, and deletes the browsing
history, cookies, site data and cached files of all time. Meanwhile a
full-screen overlay shows the wiggling CromIKO mascot and a flickering
flame; at the end a new tab opens and a toast confirms it.

Bookmarks, passwords and settings are kept. The deleted data types are
the same as Chromium's "Delete browsing data" item, including its
policy that can keep the history.

